Warning [jet.UnusedParameter]: Parameter `value` is never used.
  --> unused_code.jet:1:22
    |
  1 | fn ignored_parameter(value: Int) -> Int { 1 }
    |                      ^^^^^
 Why: An unused parameter often means the function contract or implementation is incomplete; Jet keeps this warning-only so prototypes stay unblocked.
 Fix: Use `value`, rename it to `_value` when it is intentionally unused, or remove it from the function contract.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0102

Warning [jet.UnusedLocalBinding]: Local binding `unused_thing` is never read.
  --> unused_code.jet:10:5
    |
 10 |     unused_thing :: 42
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A binding that no later expression reads adds dead code and may hide a computed result that should have been used.
 Fix: Remove the binding when its initializer is side-effect free, or rename `unused_thing` to `_unused_thing` when the value must be computed.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0101

Warning [jet.UnusedPrivateFn]: Private function `unused_helper` is never called or used as a value.
  --> unused_code.jet:4:8
    |
  4 |     fn unused_helper() -> Int { 1 }
    |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A private function with no reachable reference is dead code; public functions stay exempt because other modules may use them.
 Fix: Remove the function, or rename `unused_helper` to `_unused_helper` when it is intentional.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0104
